# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' installer default (core.autocrlf=true) gives a
# Windows clone a CRLF working tree, and `gofmt -l cmd internal` then reports
# every Go file in the repository as unformatted — gofmt's output is LF-only,
# so scripts/build.sh fails at its first stage with a list of 300 files and no
# hint that line endings are the cause. The shell scripts and the Dockerfiles
# have the same requirement for a different reason: they are copied into Linux
# images, where a CRLF shebang line makes the interpreter unfindable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, so a font or an image is not corrupted by
# newline translation on the way in or out.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.wasm binary
